# B008: exact-oracle Algorithm1 correctness and resource reference

Prospective after B007. Primary source paper.pdf AppendixA.1 Algorithm1 pp15–16. Hypothesis: accuracy-linked pruning and predecessor queries repair the query-contract gap on this native stream, at increased retention cost. This is a reproduction/control, not a new algorithm or theorem refutation.

Use the same held-out-in-time last500items of B005, no independent randomness. Norm target L3, desired smoothing alpha=.1, exact per-copy ALG so sampling epsilon=0. Set beta=alpha^3/3. Derivation: if ||b||p >= (1-beta)||a||p for a=b+d coordinatewise, then ||d||p^p <= ||a||p^p-||b||p^p <= p beta ||a||p^p. Minkowski and monotonicity after common nonnegative suffix c yield ||a+c||p-||b+c||p <=(p beta)^(1/p)||a+c||p, hence alpha=.1. This norm-specific sufficient beta avoids confusing Fp with its root.

Implement exact per-copy Counter+integerF3, start everyarrival, update all, then use literal Algorithm1 pruning: choose largest k with norm(k)>=(1-beta)norm(ell); remove surviving indices in (ell,k-1] (integer index k-1, so keep k); advanceell=k; stop when no later eligible k. Do not cap20 or change beta after seeing results. Queries return largest retained start <=target (zero-based translation). Keep exact normative Algorithm1 text/source audit for the potential k=ell termination case; this is stopping scan when no later eligible copy exists, not dropping future births.

At everyarrival test all valid W in[1,2,3,8,16,32,64,128,256,500] using independent Counter truth (fewer than5000 full-length checks early). At finalarrival test everyW1..500. Record all errors, selectedstarts, retentioncounts, exact copycounterstate memory samples at t100,250,500, peaklogicalentries, update/prune/query wallseconds, validationtime separate, full processRSS andtime. Preserve all violations >.1+1e-12 without aborting; abort only arithmetic inconsistency. Baselines are B006 native query errors and exact fixedW counters on exactly the same input, but do not infer fair speedup because arbitraryW/exactoracle is stronger and per-copy counters are deliberate correctness controls. Tasktimeout120s, cpu_guard4GiB,expected<150MiB. Next decision: if accuratebutnearfullretention, focus on cost of the oracle/sketch and faithful sampling assumptions, not a20copy capped benchmark. If accuracy fails inspect literalpruning before any expansion.
